ProDOS 8 Loader Code Expansion Notes  by Monte BenareshMay 19, 1989Revised May 23, 1989 by Monte BenareshABOUT THIS DOCUMENTThis document contains my log of steps taken to expand the "loader" portion of the"P8" file on the GS/OSª System Disk.  This portion of code gets executed when P8 isloaded into the machine and is then discarded once ProDOS is installed into the machine(assuming the installation is successful).  This code includes special-cased routinesto set up the environment and to relocate the various drivers and managers to theirfinal execution locations.  This code also displays the splash screen, identifiesonline devices, and loads the ".SYSTEM" file.The loader portion of the code is of predefined size and is currently $B00 bytes long.This fact is hard-coded in some of the P8 sourcecode and in the makefile, so expansionof this area is a non-trivial task that presently requires some changes to be made byhand.  This document is intended to be a log of those changes so that subsequentattempts to expand the loader section will require the engineer to merely use thisdocument as a cookbook-type guide.  Better yet, the aforementioned interdependenciescould be bound by the build system so that expansion of the loader portion would beautomated.This task is motivated by a need to make room for a patch which will support programswhich run under ProDOS 8 and which make QuickDraw2 calls.  This patch fixes a bug inthe 5.0 System Disk where QuickDraw makes GS/OSª calls without first checking that theSystem is installed in the machine.  The patch installs code which is vectored intothe GS/OSª entry points and returns an error for GS/OSª calls.  This fixes thingsbecause QuickDraw handles errors properly.The patch is run during the load/setup phase of starting P8.  The loader code checksthat the current machine is a GS and that P8 is being booted directly, i.e., notbeing installed by GQuit.  The patch disables interrupts (for no specific reason,only as a precaution), switches the machine to native mode, allocates memory forthe "real" GS/OS patch, copies that code into the allocated memory, sets up bothGS/OSª entry points to point to their appropriate pieces of the code, restores theenvironment and then returns to the P8 loader code.This change is documented in rev note #101 in the P8 mlisrc.aii file.NOTESfile; PROC; location				changes--------------------				-------ram.n; PROC RAM1; label "SRCE" (2 places)	"EQU $2B00" becomes "EQU $2C00"ram.n; PROC RAM2; proc header			"ORG $2B00" becomes "ORG $2C00"mlisrc.aii; before PROC PROCONE; label "ram_1"	"equ mli_0+$b00" becomes "equ mli_0+$C00"						Hex addresses in comments on following						equates should be updated.mlisrc.aii; PROC PROCONE; label "ram_1"		exact duplicate of above changemlisrc.aii; PROC PROCONE; label "loader_end"	from here to the end of the proc (ENDP):							"$B00" becomes "$C00"							"$2B00" becomes "$2C00"make.p8; build commands for "ram.bin"		"-lseg RAM2 -org $002B00" becomes						"-lseg RAM2 -org $002C00"make.p8; build commands for "{workfolder}p8"	in "Overlayiigs" commands, all hex values						after a "-a" directive must be augmented						by $100, e.g., "-a $2F36" becomes						"-a $3036"